{{!-- What the steading pays each season to keep what it has built.

      The watch's Surplus "or it disbands", the weapons the smith maintains each spring, the militia's
      week of practice, the logging camp's keep. Not a step of Seasons Change — nothing in the move
      says any of it — so it is not numbered among the steps, and not left in the general list either,
      where a bill read exactly like a payout.

      Its own section, outside the procedure and before what the season owes, because it is the one
      part of the turn the steading brings on itself. Each line keeps its control: these are plain
      arithmetic, and the season's own Apply still writes them, since the section they moved to is
      still this season's.

      Params: statement (TurnoverStatement). --}}
{{#if statement.upkeep.length}}
	<div class="steading-upkeep">
		<h4 class="steading-upkeep-label">{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.upkeep"}}</h4>
		{{!-- The batch, because this is what it writes. "Apply the season" used to sit under the general
		      list, which now holds only clauses the sheet cannot write — a button under rows it does
		      not touch, and none under the rows it does. It still applies everything the season owes,
		      and its totals still say what that comes to. --}}
		{{> "stonetop.steading-statement" statement=statement automaticLines=statement.upkeep
		    showSource=true showDelta=true applyAllAction="applyTurnover"
		    applyAllLabel="stonetop.steading.effects.applySeason"}}
	</div>
{{/if}}
